# ---- dihedrals ----
# v2: switched to AceDRG's atom-choice convention. τ(Cγ-Cβ=Cα-SG) = 180° is
# equivalent to my original τ(SG-Cβ=Cα-C7carbonyl) = 0° (syn-addition geometry),
# but the Cγ-anchored version is what AceDRG emits and matches CCP4-ML convention.
# period=2 + σ=5° lets refinement choose syn vs anti when 8FD9-like data has
# already pushed the model to τ=-89° before the link CIF was applied; the
# planarity restraint below provides the binding sp2 constraint.
#
# AceDRG also adds a soft τ on the Cα-Cβ-SG-CB single-bond hinge (sp3-sp2),
# period=3, σ=20° — keeps the local geometry stable without locking the Cys
# sidechain orientation. Pure-quality-of-life restraint.
loop_
_chem_link_tor.id
_chem_link_tor.atom_1_comp_id
_chem_link_tor.atom_id_1
_chem_link_tor.atom_2_comp_id
_chem_link_tor.atom_id_2
