# =====================================================================
# Ligand-side modification — POST-PRODUCT CROTONAMIDE INPUT BRANCH.
#
# Assumes the ligand chem_comp was deposited with the C=C already drawn
# (XQQ-style — see PDB entry 8FD9). Just delete the spare H on Cβ that's
# being replaced by the new SG bond.
#
# v2 (2026-06-07): the v1 plane-delete block over {Cβ, Cα, C7, N, O} was
# removed. The link's PLN_VINYL plane is now scoped to just {SG, Cβ, Cα, Cγ}
# (per AceDRG convention), so it no longer overlaps the ligand's amide
# plane and the deletion is unnecessary. The conjugated π system is held
# by the standalone amide plane (in the ligand chem_comp) + the new
# PLN_VINYL plane — they share Cα but don't conflict.
#
# AceDRG-derived bond-order + retype changes (from cys-xqq_link.cif mod_XQQm1):
#   * Cα-Cβ stays double 1.34 (Å). AceDRG's value of 1.371 reflects CSD vinyl-
#     thioether average; I keep 1.34 since the ligand chem_comp already has
#     it correctly for the canonical post-product form.
#   * No retype of Cβ — it stays C/CR1 (sp2 vinyl). Mod2 is a single delete.
#
# If the runtime detector instead matched the alkyne-pre form (free drug
# SMILES, R-C≡C-C(=O)-N), use the §A.2-style variant block which:
#   (1) changes Cα≡Cβ from triple to double bond,
#   (2) adds a new H on Cα,
#   (3) retypes Cα and Cβ from sp to sp2.
# See CYS-YNA-mod2-alkyne.cif (sibling template) for that variant.
# =====================================================================
data_mod_CYS-YNA-mod2
loop_
_chem_mod_atom.mod_id
_chem_mod_atom.function
_chem_mod_atom.atom_id
_chem_mod_atom.new_atom_id
